  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sierra Nevada's federal contracting activity in FY2026 to date totals $1.9B in contract obligations across 39 awards, with an average award size of $49.2M. Obligations are down 14.5% year over year. The Department of Defense accounts for the full $1.9B in reported obligations for the period. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sierra Nevada, with $1.5B in obligations, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services with $333M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing with $115M. Historical fiscal-year obligations show a rise from $112M in FY21 to $2.2B in FY25, then $1.9B in FY26. Smaller markets include Computer Systems Design Services at $4.7M, All Other Telecommunications at $3.8M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $2.7M, and Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $20K. The Department of Homeland Security is a minor buyer with $35K in obligations for the period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Sierra Nevada's top buyers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer for Sierra Nevada, with $1.9B in obligations. The Department of Homeland Security is also listed, with $35K in obligations. No other agencies are reported in the top-buyers list for the period. The buying profile is heavily concentrated in defense obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products does Sierra Nevada sell to the government?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sierra Nevada, with $1.5B in obligations. Professional, scientific, and technical services related work is significant, with All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $333M. Related manufacturing and systems work appears in Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $115M and several smaller NAICS categories ranging from $4.7M down to $20K."
      }
    ]
